{{--
  One label, as it appears everywhere a label appears.

  A pill is three lines of markup and it was already written four times: on the
  issue, on the new-issue form, in the label editor, and now on the list row.
  The one that matters is the colour pair - a label's background is chosen by a
  person and the text on it has to stay readable against whatever they chose -
  and four copies of that is four places for one of them to be wrong.

  `textColor` is computed by `labelTextColor` in `app/Actions/Issue/labels`,
  where it is tested. A component imports nothing, so the view passes it in.
--}}
<span class="label-pill" style="background: #{{ label.color }}; color: {{ label.textColor }};">
  {{ label.name }}
</span>

<style>
  .label-pill {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 2px 9px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.5;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
